+# Ops Control v1.5.1 — Deployment Runbook
+
+This runbook covers Phase 2 Day 1 rollout. Follow each section in order; do not skip
+the smoke tests.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Mac operator workstation (admin / sales / quality)
+
+**Target**: macOS 12+ on Apple Silicon (arm64).
+
+1. Copy `OpsControl-Client-v1.5.1-mac-arm64.dmg` to the operator's Mac.
+2. Double-click the DMG → drag **OpsControl CLIENT** to `/Applications`.
+3. Launch from Launchpad (the first launch may show a Gatekeeper prompt — right-click
+   the app, choose **Open**, then confirm).
+4. The smart-client setup wizard runs on first launch:
+   - **Embedded mode** (default): server runs in-process — no remote connection needed.
+   - **Thin mode**: point at the production server URL (e.g. `http://10.102.3.61:3000`).
+
+**Smoke test (matches DMG v13 hardware-test plan that passed 6/6)**:
+- [ ] App launches without "ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED" or splash crash
+- [ ] Login screen renders; demo creds work (`demo / demo1234`)
+- [ ] Standard Calc tab loads (verifies SQLite + UI bundle)
+- [ ] Layout PDF preview renders in Standard Calc (verifies PR #16 cherry-pick)
+- [ ] RFQ Tracker drawer stays stable through ≥1 60-second auto-refresh tick (verifies PR #16 snapshot)
+- [ ] Sidebar logo click returns to Home (verifies PR #18 click-to-Home)
+
+**Rollback**: keep `desktop/dist-electron-v13/OpsControl-Server-v1.5.1-mac-arm64.dmg`
+(SHA256 `628270e6dc5a2fd79933fccd941a6227442ea46df18e35a88ba4794259f8cd72`) on hand.
+Drop new DMG out of `/Applications`, install v13 from the rollback file.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Windows kiosk (shop floor)
+
+**Target**: Windows 10/11 x64.
+
+1. Copy `OpsControl-Client-v1.5.1-win-x64.exe` to the kiosk PC (USB or shared folder).
+2. Run as Administrator → NSIS wizard → choose install location (default
+   `%LocalAppData%\Programs\OpsControl CLIENT`).
+3. Allow the desktop shortcut + Start Menu entry.
+4. First launch — same setup wizard as Mac:
+   - For shop-floor kiosks pointing at the central server, choose **Thin mode** + server
+     URL `http://10.102.3.61:3000`.
+
+**Smoke test**:
+- [ ] App launches without DLL-load failure or "module not found"
+- [ ] Login + Standard Calc same as Mac
+- [ ] Hardware: scanner / serial label printer detected (Hardware tab in Settings)
+
+**If launch fails with `better_sqlite3.node` error**: this build's native binary is
+PE32+ x86-64. Verify with `file resources\app\node_modules\better-sqlite3\build\Release\better_sqlite3.node`
+inside the install dir. If the binary is wrong, build on a Windows host (see §4).
+
+**Rollback**: each Windows install keeps the previous `app.asar` in
+`%LocalAppData%\Programs\OpsControl CLIENT\resources\` if the user ran v1.5.0 first.
+Otherwise reinstall the previous v1.5.0 EXE from the offsite backup.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Production server (remote Windows at 10.102.3.61:3000)
+
+**Important**: this is a **Node.js Express server**, NOT a packaged Electron app.
+Deploys via `deploy.ps1` from the repo working tree.
+
+**Pre-deploy checklist**:
+- [ ] Confirm the deploy.ps1 target IP in the script header (`$ServerHost`)
+- [ ] Confirm `OPS_TOTP_KEY` is preserved in remote `.env` (Sprint 1.7 gate; misset key
+      bricks every user's 2FA — see CLAUDE.md "TOTP key rotation runbook")
+- [ ] Confirm latest backup exists in `\\<server>\backups\ops-control\` and is < 24h old
+- [ ] Run `npm run preflight` locally to validate the env
+
+**Deploy steps**:
+1. From a Windows admin workstation with PowerShell:
+   ```powershell
+   cd C:\Path\To\Ops Control v1.2
+   git checkout main
+   git pull
+   git rev-parse HEAD   # confirm = ccf49fe or newer
+   .\deploy.ps1 -ServerHost user@10.102.3.61
+   ```
+2. The script:
+   - Snapshots live `/opt/ops-control` to `/opt/ops-control/releases/<timestamp>/` (5-snapshot retention)
+   - MERGES new `.env` into existing (preserves `OPS_TOTP_KEY`)
+   - Runs preflight gate; aborts on validation failure
+   - Stops the service, rsyncs new code, starts the service
+3. Watch the logs:
+   ```powershell
+   ssh user@10.102.3.61 "Get-EventLog -LogName Application -Source 'NSSM' -Newest 30"
+   # Or the service log file directly
+   ```
+4. Confirm `🔐 TOTP boot probe OK — N user(s) enrolled, key fp …` in the boot log.
+
+**Smoke test (production)**:
+- [ ] `curl http://10.102.3.61:3000/health` returns `{"status":"ok",...}`
+- [ ] `curl http://10.102.3.61:3000/ready` returns 200
+- [ ] Login from a browser at `http://10.102.3.61:3000/`
+- [ ] Existing user can pass 2FA (proves OPS_TOTP_KEY preserved)
+- [ ] Quote History loads (proves SQLite + Library/ data intact)
+
+**Rollback bad deploy** (per CLAUDE.md "Bad deploy" runbook):
+```powershell
+ssh user@10.102.3.61
+sudo systemctl stop ops-control   # or: nssm stop ops-control
+ls /opt/ops-control/releases       # pick previous timestamp dir
+PREV=20260508-200000               # immediately before the bad deploy
+cd /opt/ops-control
+cp -R releases/$PREV/server releases/$PREV/client releases/$PREV/scripts ./
+cp releases/$PREV/package.json releases/$PREV/package-lock.json ./
+sudo systemctl start ops-control
+```
+
+---
+
+## 4. Build Windows EXE on a Windows host (fallback)
+
+The Mac-host cross-build that produced `releases/v1.5.1/OpsControl-*-win-x64.exe` works
+because better-sqlite3 ships prebuilt PE32+ x64 binaries via npm. If a future native
+dep doesn't have prebuilds, cross-build from Mac will fail with
+`node-gyp does not support cross-compiling native modules from source`.
+
+In that case, build on Windows directly:
+
+```powershell
+# On a Windows 10/11 x64 dev machine with Node 24 + Visual Studio Build Tools 2022
+cd C:\Build\OpsControl
+git clone https://github.com/thiepdanghd82/Ops-Control.git .
+git checkout v1.5.1   # tag once production validates
+cd client && npm install && npx vite build && cd ..
+cd desktop
+npm install   # rebuilds natives for Windows + Electron
+$env:OPS_BUILD_ROLE="Server"
+npx electron-builder --win --x64 `
+  --config.extraMetadata.opsMode=server `
+  --config.productName="OpsControl SERVER" `
+  --config.npmRebuild=false
+$env:OPS_BUILD_ROLE="Client"
+npx electron-builder --win --x64 `
+  --config.extraMetadata.opsMode=client `
+  --config.productName="OpsControl CLIENT" `
+  --config.npmRebuild=false
+```
+
+Both EXEs land in `desktop\dist-electron\`. Run the Lesson 28 hash check on each:
+```powershell
+Get-FileHash "dist-electron\win-unpacked\resources\app\node_modules\better-sqlite3\build\Release\better_sqlite3.node" -Algorithm SHA256
+Get-FileHash "dist-electron\win-unpacked\resources\app.asar.unpacked\node_modules\better-sqlite3\build\Release\better_sqlite3.node" -Algorithm SHA256
+```
+Both hashes must be identical.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Multi-client LAN smoke test
+
+Once one Mac is running the SERVER variant successfully:
+
+1. **Mac A** (server): launch `OpsControl SERVER`, choose **Embedded** mode. Note the IP
+   shown in the About panel (e.g. `192.168.1.42:3000`).
+2. **Mac B** (client): launch `OpsControl CLIENT`, choose **Thin** mode, point at
+   `http://192.168.1.42:3000`.
+3. Verify:
+   - [ ] Mac B login screen loads (no CORS / connection-refused)
+   - [ ] Mac B can save a quote → Mac A's Quote History shows it within 60s (SSE push)
+   - [ ] Mac A can transition an approval → Mac B sees the new state on next refresh
+
+This proves the SERVER + CLIENT split works end-to-end on the same wire that production
+will use.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Tagging the release
+
+After production smoke test confirms green:
+
+```bash
+cd "/Volumes/Macintosh Data/Claude-Cowork/3. PROJECTS/Ops Control v1.2"
+git checkout main
+git pull
+git tag -a v1.5.1 ccf49fe -m "Phase 1 final — 21 PRs + 14 critical fixes"
+git push origin v1.5.1
+```
+
+The tag becomes the immutable provenance for `releases/v1.5.1/SHA256SUMS.txt`. Future
+audits can prove every shipped binary traces back to commit `ccf49fe` on `main`.
+
+If a user-visible change lands between this build and tagging, bump the version in
+`package.json` to `1.5.2` first, rebuild, and tag the new commit.
+
+---
+
+## Known good rollback targets
+
+| Version | SHA256 of Mac arm64 SERVER DMG | Build SHA |
+|---|---|---|
+| v13 (hardware-tested) | `628270e6dc5a2fd79933fccd941a6227442ea46df18e35a88ba4794259f8cd72` | `7a83682` |
+| v14 (this release) | `737808e7b9f6a324a21b0191113300dca0b40cb7591d1601f6e2e078484c46e3` | `ccf49fe` |
+
+Keep both DMGs on hand for at least 7 days post-rollout.
