+Ops Control v1.5.1 — DMG v16 verifyBackup root-cause fix
+=========================================================
+Built:        2026-05-08T14:42:00Z (Mac arm64 host)
+Built from:   fix/day1-regressions-printer-sse-backup @ 72a48e4682c66c539063afd9e19c503cb79d6411
+PR:           https://github.com/thiepdanghd82/Ops-Control/pull/22 (additive commit)
+Build env:    Node v24.15.0, Electron 41.3.0, better-sqlite3 12.9.0
+Status:       UNMERGED — for hardware-test verification
+
+What changed vs DMG v15
+-----------------------
+1 additional commit (72a48e4): backupOpsDb now returns BOTH `file`
+(basename, legacy) and `path` (absolute, new). runBackupCycle's
+verify step uses `path` instead of `file`.
+
+Root cause that DMG v15 still had
+---------------------------------
+verifyBackup was being called with a basename like
+"ops_20260508_142439.sqlite". SQLite resolves relative paths
+against process.cwd() which on packaged Electron is APP_ROOT
+(inside the read-only signed .app bundle). The basename did not
+exist there, so SQLite threw "unable to open database file".
+
+DMG v15 already had:
+- Cosmetic UI path display fix (PKG_BACKUP_DIR → getPkgBackupDir())
+- Printer macOS branch (lpstat / lp)
+- SSE auth via getTokenFromHeader
+
+DMG v16 adds the actual runBackupCycle fix on top.
+
+Lesson 28 ABI verification
+--------------------------
+Both DMGs pass: app/node_modules/better-sqlite3/.../better_sqlite3.node
+                AND app.asar.unpacked/.../better_sqlite3.node
+                hash to e8c5e5e4b5b2b8fec4eeaf3ca18df78d40271bde738ec57faddb19bcedda5eb1
+
+Test plan
+---------
+1. Settings → Backup / Restore → "Run now"
+   Expected: succeeds, last run shows ✓ OK
+   If it still says "unable to open database file": runtime trace
+   needed (would point to a different undiscovered step).
+
+2. Other v15 fixes still verified:
+   - Diagnostics → "Liệt kê máy in" → printer list (or empty)
+   - Diagnostics → "SSE event stream" → 200 + "ready"
+   - Backup path display = <userData>/data/Backup/PackageBackups/Data
+
